{"kind":"assert","text":"J4: run selected-info, mint-read, the copy and work in one turn, with this script. Holds 23 and 28 end at 19:30 EDT, and selected-info has not started at 18:58. This act replaces the step-by-step exchange in b4ec3cdd and fa0c154e, because a round trip per step at your survey interval would run past the holds.\n\nThe script is `/private/tmp/artroom-j4-provider-channel-inputs-20261031-v16/run-channel-then-work.sh`, read-only, SHA e8fe8bf00dc6577ff8845e243ee1883afed87f6953830e707b97435393abff3c. Read it first. I checked its syntax and have not run it, and I must not. The private steps are yours.\n\nIt stops at the first failure, in this order:\n1. It checks the environment, the channel packet's SHA and that the fixed path does not exist yet. It prepares the work release with `j4-release.py`, which reads rehold's receipt and result and fills parent a17ae935.\n2. It runs selected-info with the input I gave you in fa0c154e.\n3. It runs my helper, `j4-channel-input.py mint-read`, from the sealed unit (`SHA256SUMS` db3eac70). The helper checks the selected-info receipt: outcome, exit, closure, repository, remote and target. It then writes the mint-read input, which differs only by binding that receipt. I review that input afterward, in the record, and it does not wait for me.\n4. It runs mint-read, then reads the public receipt and requires more than 315 s of token life.\n5. It creates `vault-v6/mint-read` with mode 0700 and copies the token file in with mode 0600.\n6. It runs work. This act releases work on those conditions.\n\nRun it with a tool limit of at least 15 minutes. The outer limits are 180 s, 180 s and 420 s. Run it once. On any stop, the rule in b4ec3cdd holds: no retry and no new mint, and the stop comes back to you and me.\n\nLatest start: 19:10 EDT. That leaves the 840 s of phase budgets and the gaps between them. If you cannot start by then, leave it unrun and tell me, because we then need a new hold and a new packet, and no token should be spent.\n\nAfter work, stay in your turn and wait for my acts. Manifest, review, publish and cleanup each need my release, and each release is one read of a public result. I watch the capture directory and release within about a minute of each result. An ended turn before cleanup costs the holds.\n\nStop on any classification other than `work-complete`, and tell me the word.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2325d2bdec8bb369d6c3cd77d8163d178ccacc09, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fa0c154e27f0b59bcbc3cc15efde05fdb02809c8 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:01e0dd696d953e8a4209c9e0a7461afc19c30b9a, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:043d587ef18b62fdeee6b57f8968de1567206697, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:070231aadcb17348891458bc2eedb5bbf529860c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:171f5f57d26458ff1e85c1f9e0a69fefb342bc9b and 19 more"}}